# Registry mapping only — deliberately NO _authToken here.
#
# npm reads .npmrc from the current directory only; it does not walk up to the
# repo root. The `netlify` and `install-all` scripts install this package with
# `cd packages/<pkg> && npm install`, so without this line the
# @ericpitcock/epicenter-icons-* dependency resolves against npmjs.org and 404s.
# That is not hypothetical: it broke the Netlify build the first time this
# package declared an @ericpitcock dependency.
#
# Auth is NOT set here. It used to be, as `_authToken=${VITE_APP_GITHUB_TOKEN}`,
# and that broke every developer machine: with the variable unset the
# substitution resolves to an empty string, and an empty token in project config
# outranks the real one in ~/.npmrc — so `npm publish` and `npm install` both
# 401 from this directory. CI gets its token from scripts/ci-npm-auth.sh, which
# writes to the user config; developers use their own ~/.npmrc.
@ericpitcock:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com/

# Keep the release-age delay for third-party packages, never for our own —
# otherwise every build in the days after a publish fails with ETARGET
# "no matching version with a date before <date>" and looks like a broken release.
min-release-age-exclude[]=@ericpitcock/*
